        answer: "ICC 500, the national storm shelter standard. It sets the 250-mph design wind speed for Oklahoma's tornado region, debris-impact testing for walls, roofs, and doors, minimum floor area per occupant, ventilation, lighting, and accessibility requirements, and peer review for larger shelters. Oklahoma school shelters are designed, reviewed, and inspected against this standard, and compliance documentation is part of the permit submittal.",
