        answer: "The base flood elevation is the computed height floodwater is expected to reach during the 1%-annual-chance (100-year) flood, shown on FEMA Flood Insurance Rate Maps. Iowa floodplain designs key everything off this number: lowest floors must sit above it (plus any local freeboard), and dry-floodproofing must protect the building up to it. An elevation certificate documents the as-built heights relative to this elevation.",
