        question: "What is the difference between detention and retention?",
        answer: "Detention temporarily stores stormwater and releases it at a controlled rate through an outlet structure — the basin drains dry between storms. Retention holds a permanent pool of water and releases only overflows. In the Des Moines area, detention is more common for meeting peak-flow limits, while retention or extended detention adds water-quality treatment by holding the first flush longer.",
